From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:29:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: show reactions on the message they react to

The LuneOS IM transport (imlibpurpletransport) drives libpurple headless
for the webOS Messaging app, which shows a reaction on the bubble it
belongs to. A received reaction is emitted as the process-wide signal
"webos-im-reaction" (account, target message id, emoji or "" when it
was removed, sender) instead of a "reacted with X" message.

To let the transport find the target later, the WhatsApp id of each
received message, and in a 1:1 chat of our own messages sent from
another device, is stashed on the conversation as "webos-msg-id" right before
serv_got_im/serv_got_chat_in.

Reactions from the app arrive through "webos-im-send-reaction" and go
out through BuildReaction(). The original sender of the target message
comes from the message cache or, failing that, from the transport
("webos-reaction-target-sender" on the account).

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
